  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added an explicit-shape ExactMatrixData scalar snapshot and ordinary same-source Python implementations of Sage-oriented partial/nonzero-pivot LU, full/reduced exact QR, and exact row Gram-Schmidt. The production module executes unchanged in CPython and Sage.js: a real Sage.js witness reconstructs all three decompositions over QQ. The contracts fix A=P*L*U, A=Q*R, and A=M*G tuple order; rectangular, rank-deficient, singular, dependent-row, and zero-dimensional shapes; caller-supplied exact square roots; and deterministic 40x40 baselines. Fraction is confined to the CPython oracle and benchmark adapters. Gram-Schmidt uses O(m*r + r*n) storage, demonstrated by a 20,000x2 regression whose peak traced allocation remains below 32MB. Live SageMath 10.9.post1 probes supply exact LU/QR/Gram fixtures and shape oracles. Nothing is wired into public Matrix yet.",
    "risks": [
      "The scalar-generic core implements bilinear inner products only. It is suitable for QQ and compatible exact real fields; complex exact fields require a separate scalar protocol with explicit conjugation before QR or Gram-Schmidt is wired publicly.",
      "The helper currently fixes Sage's default PLU tuple contract for explicit partial/nonzero pivoting. Public Matrix.LU still needs an adapter for pivot=None auto-selection and the optional compact return format.",
      "Earlier aggregate attempts exposed a missing worktree-local M4RI prefix and one contention-sensitive inherited ZZ density_500 measurement above its budget. Rebuilding the content-addressed native caches repaired the stale prefix; the final aggregate passed all FFI, sanitizer lifecycle, compiler, migration, and performance gates, with ZZ density_500 at 3.00ms against its 8ms budget."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "In the integration lane, add src/lib/sagejs/linear_algebra/decompositions.py to pyrightconfig.json and test/linear-decomposition-contract.cjs to test/node-test-manifest.cjs. The existing linear-algebra-algorithms prefix already owns the source, so no package-graph entry is needed.",
      "Wire Matrix.LU, Matrix.QR, and Matrix.gram_schmidt through a lazy sagejs.linear_algebra.decompositions import. For ZZ and QQ, bulk-export once into ExactMatrixData with QQ(0) and QQ(1), supply a checked exact square-root callback for QR/orthonormal Gram-Schmidt, and construct each returned Matrix over the intended fraction or exact-real field with the recorded explicit dimensions; preserve Sage's pivot=None, compact-format, mutability/cache, and exception behavior in the public adapter.",
      "After public differential tests are stable, benchmark each method and replace only measured hot paths with generated FLINT resources or source-transparent typed Python while retaining these ordinary-Python contracts as the oracle."
    ]
  }
}
